/Title (Steps of the Code Step 1: Create the order class The order class contains two private variables: date number These represent the order date and order number. Because they are private, this demonstrates encapsulation. Step 2: Create the order constructor The constructor initializes: date number using: this.date = date; this.number = number; Step 3: Create confirm\(\) method confirm\(\) displays the order number and confirmation date. Step 4: Create close\(\) method close\(\) displays that the order has been closed. Step 5: Create specialorder class specialorder extends order This means specialorder inherits from order. It has an additional method: dispatch\(\) which displays that the special order has been dispatched. Step 6: Create normalorder class normalorder extends order This class also inherits from order. It has two additional methods: dispatch\(\) receive\(\) Step 7: Create customer The customer class has: name location Both are private. It contains: sendorder\(\) receiveorder\(\) Step 8: sendorder\(\) receives an order public void sendorder\(order order\) Notice that the parameter type is order. Therefore, an object of a child class such as specialorder can also be passed. Step 9: receiveorder\(\) receives an order void receiveorder\(order order\) It displays that the customer received the order and then calls: order.close\(\); Step 10: Create customer object customer c = new customer\("hemanth", "vizag"\); Step 11: Create special order specialorder so =     new specialorder\("12th august", "44"\); Step 12: Send special order c.sendorder\(so\); The customer sends the special order. Step 13: Dispatch special order so.dispatch\(\); Step 14: Receive special order c.receiveorder\(so\); The order is received and then closed. Step 15: Create normal order normalorder no =     new normalorder\("13th august", "82"\); Step 16: Process normal order The program: Receives the order. Closes the order. Dispatches the order. Receives it. Calls receiveorder\(\) again.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 632 0 R
/Next 636 0 R
>>
endobj
635 0 obj
<<
